<title>BRAZIL: Brazil buys dollars at 1.0590 in commercial market.</title>
<headline>Brazil buys dollars at 1.0590 in commercial market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank bought dollars at 1.0590 reais each in a buy tender in the commercial foreign exchange market, dealers said.</p>
<p>The result of the auction kept the local currency within the new real-dollar mini-band set this morning at 1.0590 to 1.0640 reais per dollar.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
